<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">Hi Sam,</span></p=
>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">So I have filled =
the May Welcome Center position just this morning, but I do still have a Si=
te Maintenance position available for May if you are interested in that.&nb=
sp;
</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">As for the open R=
anger positions, what will be posted is going to be the entry level Seasona=
l Ranger Assistant positions, which will not have the same level of require=
ments as the full time Ranger positions,
 so generally most of the Rangers, myself included, start off as Ranger Ass=
istants that are hired seasonally for the busy summer months.&nbsp; It help=
s you to get a grasp on how operations work from the park staff=92s side of=
 things and helps to build those skills
 that are essential for getting the full time Ranger Jobs.&nbsp; A job that=
 is also posted as a =93Seasonal Ranger=94 would mean it is still on the sa=
me level as a Full time Park Ranger, but they have a few months off during =
the calendar year, so it is still a higher-level
 position than a Seasonal Ranger Assistant. </span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">The Seasonal Rang=
er Assistant positions should be getting posted on the Workday website in t=
he next week or so, so definitely keep an eye out for them.&nbsp; It would =
be under the Parks &amp; Recreation category,
 which will then list the Park that has posted the Seasonal Assistant Posit=
ions.&nbsp;
</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">If you were to ge=
t a Ranger Assistant position it does complicate being a Park Host, as you =
cannot do both at the same time, and would then have to find a different pl=
ace to reside as Park Staff are not
 given campsites to live in like the Park Hosts.&nbsp; The Host site is par=
t of the package of being a volunteer as it is an unpaid position, but if y=
ou were to become a paid employee, such as a Ranger Assistant, then you wil=
l have to find your own place to reside
 outside of the campground.&nbsp; You are still allowed to camp at the camp=
ground as a paid employee, but you would be just a regular visitor at that =
point and subject to all of the stay limits that we have for our regular gu=
ests (State Parks have a 14 day stay
 limit for our campers which does not apply to Park Hosts).</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">Hopefully that ad=
ds some clarity.</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">&nbsp;</span></p>
